```
Fine-tuning modes:
`full` — retrain everything (most power, most risk of overwriting old skills)
`adapter` — small add-on layers learn new skill, base frozen (safe, cheap, reversible)
`head-only` — retrain just the final output layer
`lora` — lightweight low-rank adaptation
`prompt-tuning` — learn an optimized prefix, no weight changes
`distillation` — student model learns from a teacher model's outputs
Fine-tune diff report — auto-summary of behavior change vs the base model
Fine-tuning individual attached skills (see Skills section) without touching the base model or other skills
