10. Merging Models — Communication & Bridging
Two independently trained models don't share a representation space — some bridge is required, latency-free direct communication isn't realistic.
```
qai.merge(model_a, model_b, bridge: "adapter")           // lowest latency, small trained translator
qai.merge(model_a, model_b, bridge: "shared_embedding")  // fastest at inference, needs joint training
qai.merge(model_a, model_b, bridge: "router")             // most flexible, more overhead

// User-selectable communication depth
qai.merge(model_a, model_b,
    communicate_via: "shared_embedding" | "adapter" | "router" | "raw_output_only",
    frequency: "every_layer" | "final_output_only")
```
Bridge auto-selection based on inspected input/output shapes
Latency profiler for merges — exact overhead per inference call
Cross-model attention — bridge as a small attention mechanism instead of pure translation
Merge compatibility score — compile-time estimate of how well two models will work together
