14. Multi-Role Self-Play / Co-Training
For tasks like "one sub-model asks coding questions, another answers and improves" — combined model, user-defined roles, not hardcoded names:
```
let model = qai.build("combined")
model.add_role("asker", type: "transformer", goal: "generate_questions")
model.add_role("answerer", type: "transformer", goal: "solve_task")

model.connect("asker" -> "answerer", channel: "question")
model.connect("answerer" -> "asker", channel: "feedback")

model.set_evaluator(fn(question, answer) {
    return run_code_test(answer)   // custom reward signal
})

model.train(mode: "self_play", rounds: 1000, task_domain: "coding", visualize: true)
```
Any number of roles, not just two (e.g. add a "critic" or "teacher" role)
Role skill dashboard — compare each role's performance over rounds
Difficulty auto-balancing so questions stay productively hard
Swap/freeze individual roles mid-training
Role template library (asker/answerer, teacher/student, generator/critic)
