28. Standard Accessors — Shared Across Every Technique
```
technique Technique {
    // SHARED — every technique guarantees these, same names, same shape
    fn tokens() -> [Token]
    fn weights() -> WeightSet
    fn loss() -> f64            // generic Signal underneath
    fn accuracy() -> f64
    fn parameters() -> ParamSet
    fn param_count() -> int

    // UNIQUE — each technique adds its own on top (e.g. Regression.formula(), Diffusion.denoise_steps())
}
```
`model.weights()`, `model.loss()`, `model.accuracy()`, `model.tokens()`, `model.parameters()` work identically no matter the technique — one interface that transfers everywhere, with technique-specific extras layered on top, never replacing the shared baseline.
