30. Classic ML Workflow Essentials (Gaps Filled)
```
let ensemble = qai.ensemble([model_a, model_b, model_c], method: "stacking")   // or "bagging" / "boosting"

model.search_hyperparams(method: "bayesian", trials: 50, target: "accuracy")   // grid / random / bayesian

model.cross_validate(folds: 5)

model.add_layer("dense", dropout: 0.3, regularize: "l2")   // regularization: dropout, L1/L2, batch norm
```
Learning rate schedulers — warmup, decay, cosine annealing — explicit and swappable, not just implicit inside `autotrain`
Early stopping — halts training automatically on validation performance plateau/regression (overfitting-specific, distinct from the "diminishing returns" auto-stop)
Transfer learning — an explicit named entry point on top of `finetune`, since "reuse a model trained on task A for task B" is such a common beginner pattern it deserves its own clear name/example in docs
More novel ideas:
Model "diet" mode — `model.compress(target_size: "50%")` — auto-picks the best mix of pruning/quantization/distillation to hit a size target with minimal accuracy loss
Training race mode — run two hyperparameter configs side by side on a split dashboard, racing to see which converges faster
Failure replay library — every bad failure on a live input auto-saves into a growing "hard examples" set for later retraining
