33. Security Module
```
// Data poisoning defense
let data = qai.dataset.stream("huggingface://some_dataset")
    .security_scan()   // flags outlier clusters, label-flipping patterns, duplicated adversarial samples
    .clean()

// Prompt injection defense (served/agentic models)
qai.serve(model,
    input_filter: "prompt_injection_guard",
    sandbox_tools: true)
```
Dataset poisoning scanner — `data.security_scan()` catches poisoned data before training starts
Prompt injection guard — built-in classifier screening incoming requests before they reach the model
Tool-call sandboxing — agentic tool calls run isolated by default; no unchecked filesystem/network access
Supply-chain verification — marketplace imports (techniques/skills/layers) are checksummed/signed; `qai.import()` warns on signature mismatch
Model weight tamper detection — `model.verify_integrity()` hash-checks weights against a known-good fingerprint
Differential privacy training — `model.train(privacy: "differential", epsilon: 1.0)` adds calibrated noise so training data can't be leaked
Output leakage filter — detects verbatim training-data reproduction or PII in outputs before serving
Standing automated red-teaming — `stress_test()` extended to run periodically against a live served model, not just once pre-deployment
