34. Execution-Grounded Learning (VM/Environment Connection)
```
let vm = qai.connect_vm(sandboxed: true, language: "python")

model.train(
    mode: "execution_grounded",
    environment: vm,
    task: "write a function that sorts a list",
    evaluator: fn(code) {
        let result = vm.run(code)
        return result.tests_passed && result.no_errors
    }
)
```
A model learns from real execution feedback (does the code actually run/pass tests?), not just pattern similarity — a genuine RL step beyond imitation learning, and it plugs directly into the self-play evaluator system (Section 14).
`Environment` — a pluggable interface, same pattern as `Technique`:
```
environment Environment {
    fn run(action) -> Result
    fn reset()
    fn observe() -> State
}
```
Built-ins: VM/sandbox (code), browser (web navigation), game engine (classic RL), robotic/physics simulator, spreadsheet/document environment. All models train against any of these with the same `mode: "execution_grounded"` call.
Execution trace as training signal — feed the model the actual runtime error/trace on failure, not just pass/fail
Difficulty-graduated coding curriculum — auto-escalate task complexity as pass rate improves
Multi-language VM pool — `qai.connect_vm(languages: ["python","rust","c"])`
Sandboxing here is the default safety posture, tying directly into the Security Module above
