35. Input/Output Pipeline & Multimodal Security
Receiving information — per-modality sanitization, not just text:
```
model.input_channels(["text", "image", "audio", "video", "file"])
let clean_image = qai.scan_multimodal(image, checks: ["steganography", "hidden_text", "adversarial_perturbation"])
```
Text → prompt injection guard
Images/video → steganography, hidden OCR-readable text, adversarial pixel perturbations (checked per-frame for video)
Audio → inaudible/ultrasonic embedded commands, adversarial perturbations
Files → hidden text layers, embedded scripts/macros, metadata injection
Where output gets diverted — and how to close it:
Steganographic exfiltration defense — `output.leak_scan()` checks generated artifacts for abnormal noise patterns hiding smuggled data
Agentic egress control — `model.set_egress(allowed_destinations: [...])` allowlists where actions/output can actually go, preventing a manipulated agent from being tricked into leaking data via a legitimate-looking tool call
Output volume anomaly detection — flags abnormal output volume/frequency as a sign of abuse, behavior-based rather than just a hard rate limit
More ideas:
Cross-modal consistency check — verify paired outputs (e.g. caption + image) actually agree before releasing
Provenance watermarking by default across all output modalities, not just images
Modality-specific stress testing — `stress_test()` extended to adversarial images/audio/video, not just text
