36. Output Renderer System (Capability-Checked)
```
let model = qai.build(technique: "diffusion", output_type: "video")
model.capabilities()                          // → ["video"]
model.generate(prompt).render_as("video")      // ✅ matches capability
model.generate(prompt).render_as("3d")         // ❌ clear error, no silent failure/substitution
```
```
renderer OutputRenderer {
    fn required_capability() -> String | [String]   // renderers can require multiple capabilities
    fn render(model_output) -> Artifact
}
```
Two-way capability matching — renderers declare what they need, models declare what they have; `render_as()` checks both before running
Multi-capability models — a model can genuinely support more than one output type if actually built/trained for it
Capability certification — `model.certify_capability("video")` test-generates and validates a real sample, not just a claimed label
Composite renderers — e.g. video-with-audio requires `["video","audio"]` present together
Closest-match suggestion on mismatch — error suggests the nearest real option instead of silently substituting
Custom renderer boilerplate — `qai new renderer --from="ImageRenderer" --name="MyRenderer"`, same fork-and-protect pattern as techniques
Renderer versioning for backward compatibility as output formats evolve
