38. Multi-Output Generation & Model Piping
Native joint output — one model, multiple output heads, generated from the same forward pass (contextually coherent by construction):
```
let model = qai.build(technique: "transformer")
model.add_layer("text_head", type: "classifier")
model.add_layer("image_head", type: "diffusion")
let result = model.generate(prompt).render_as(["text", "image"])
result.text
result.image
```
Piped/orchestrated output — separate specialized models chained together (how most real production multimodal systems actually work today — a language model calls out to an image model as a tool, rather than one model natively producing everything):
```
model_a.generate(prompt).pipe_to(model_b).pipe_to(model_c).render_as(["text","code","image"])
```
Orchestration is cheaper/faster to build; native joint generation requires training on paired multimodal data from the start and is architecturally "more correct" but rarer. Quantum should support both explicitly.
`Bundle` type — keeps multiple typed outputs together with linking metadata instead of loose return values:
```
type Bundle {
    text: Text?
    image: Image?
    code: Code?
    video: Video?
}
```
