42. Stateful Sessions, Auto-Checkpointing & Declarative Syntax
Fixes the "running the script again creates a brand-new model" problem, database-style:
```
let model = qai.build("regression", name: "my_model", if_exists: "resume")
// first run: creates fresh. every run after: resumes saved progress instead of starting over

model.train(data, autosave: true, autosave_interval: "every_epoch")
```
`if_exists: "resume"` (default-safe, idempotent, like `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`) vs `if_exists: "fresh"` when a clean model is actually wanted
Autosave on interval and on shutdown, so nothing is lost without an explicit save
Optional SQL-style declarative syntax — alternative front-end syntax, selected via a file directive, compiling down to the exact same underlying model definition as normal Quantum code — lets database-minded beginners and programmers both build the same thing in the syntax that matches how they think:
```
#style: declarative

CREATE MODEL sentiment_classifier
USING transformer
WITH embedding(size: 512), attention(heads: 8), classifier(output: 2)

TRAIN sentiment_classifier ON imdb_reviews UNTIL accuracy > 0.90

SELECT prediction, confidence FROM sentiment_classifier WHERE input = "great movie"
```
