43. Abilities, Knowledge Gaps & Targeted Training
Hierarchical abilities, drillable into sub-areas:
```
model.abilities()                                  // → { code_generation: 0.81, reasoning: 0.74, ... }
model.abilities().drill_down("code_generation")    // → { security: 0.42, web_dev: 0.85, ... }
model.finetune(data: security_data, focus: "code_generation.security")
```
Auto-diagnose + auto-improve loop, tied to the benchmark system:
```
let diagnosis = model.auto_diagnose()               // → weakest area found automatically
model.auto_improve(diagnosis.weakest, data: qai.dataset.stream("huggingface://secure_code_examples"))
```
Weaknesses vs. knowledge gaps — different problems, different fixes: a weakness has partial exposure and performs badly; a gap has zero exposure to a whole topic.
```
model.knowledge_map()   // → { security_code: "weak (0.42)", quantum_physics: "gap (no exposure)", cooking: "strong" }
model.finetune(data: quantum_data, mode: "adapter", new_domain: true)   // filling a genuine gap, not refining a weak skill
```
Parameters vs. hyperparameters — clarified:
```
model.hyperparameters()   // what the developer sets: layers, heads, learning rate, epochs
model.parameters()        // what training LEARNED: actual weight values — empty until training happens
```
