44. Input/Output, Freeform Output & Technique Upgrading
`Input` / `Output` — simple, symmetric naming (renamed from the earlier "receiver" — same word pattern, obvious pair), same capability-checking discipline on both sides:
```
input Input {
    fn parse(raw) -> ModelInput
}
output Output {
    fn render(model_output) -> Artifact
}
qai.input("character.obj", as: "3d")
model.generate(prompt).output("image")
```

Freeform/experimental output mode — no renderer forced, model outputs its natural raw structure, useful for research/exploration, clearly marked as advanced/experimental rather than default:
```
model.generate(prompt, format: "freeform")
```
Custom bridges remain fully open — confirmed capable of arbitrary logic (e.g. an image→code translation bridge):
```
bridge ImageToCodeBridge extends Bridge {
    fn translate(image_output) -> code_input { /* fully custom logic */ }
}
model_a.pipe_to(model_b, bridge: ImageToCodeBridge)
```
Upgrading a technique type without silently affecting existing models:
```
technique MoE_v2 extends MoE {
    fn new_capability() { ... }
}
model.upgrade_technique(MoE_v2)   // explicit opt-in per model — nothing changes automatically
```
