45. Parameter Reference — Technical Names & Simple Aliases
Every parameter has a plain-English alias alongside its technical name; both work interchangeably, and `param.help()` shows both together so beginners learn the friendly name first and pick up the standard term naturally.
```
model.set(experts: 32, active_experts: 4)   // simple alias
model.set(num_experts: 32, top_k: 4)        // technical name — identical result
```
Core (every model): `input_size/output_size` (input_dim/output_dim), `inner_size` (hidden_dim), `depth` (num_layers), `attention_heads` (num_heads), `forget_rate` (dropout), `normalize` (layer_norm), `starting_weights` (weight_init), `precision` (dtype)
Transformer/LLM: `vocabulary_size` (vocab_size), `memory_span` (max_seq_len/context_length), `model_width` (dim/d_model), `position_scale` (rope_theta), `remember_past` (kv_cache), `share_vocabulary` (tie_weights)
MoE: `expert_count` (num_experts), `active_experts` (top_k), `always_on_expert` (shared_expert), `balance_strength` (load_balancing_loss_coef), `router_randomness` (noisy_gating)
CNN: `filter_size` (kernel_size), `step_size` (stride), `downsample_method` (pooling)
Diffusion: `noise_steps` (num_timesteps), `prompt_strength` (guidance_scale)
Training/Optimizer: `learning_speed` (learning_rate), `weight_shrink` (weight_decay), `warmup_period` (warmup_steps), `gradient_limit` (gradient_clipping), `label_softness` (label_smoothing), `speed_mode` (mixed_precision), `finetune_rank/finetune_strength` (lora_r/lora_alpha)
Regression/Classification: `category_count` (num_classes), `output_style` (output_activation)
RL: `future_importance` (gamma), `exploration_rate` (epsilon), `memory_size` (replay_buffer_size)
GAN: `creator_speed/critic_speed` (generator_lr/discriminator_lr), `noise_size` (latent_dim)
RNN: `two_directions` (bidirectional), `memory_style` (cell_type — LSTM/GRU/plain)
GNN: `hop_count` (num_message_passing_layers), `combine_method` (aggregation_type)
Audio: `frequency_bands` (n_mels)
Tokenizer: `splitting_method` (vocab_method — bpe/wordpiece)
Ideas:
`qai.glossary()` — prints the entire parameter reference table (simple name, technical name, meaning, typical range) as a built-in cheat sheet
Difficulty tiers per parameter (`param.tier`: beginner/advanced) — a simplified build mode only surfaces beginner-tier params by default
Smart defaults with reasoning shown in `.help()` ("dropout defaults to 0.1 — enough to reduce overfitting without slowing learning much")
Typo-correction on parameter names ("did you mean `dropout`?")
Live parameter cheat cards in the dashboard with plain-English tooltips
