`chunk_size / chunk_overlap`	`retrieval_bite_size / retrieval_overlap`	how RAG splits documents
`top_k_retrieval`	`docs_recalled`	how many external documents get pulled in
`ssm_state_size` (Mamba)	`flow_memory_size`	state-space model's compressed running memory
`conv_kernel` (Mamba)	`local_window`	small local pattern size
`expand_factor` (Mamba)	`width_multiplier`	internal width expansion
`sparse_attention`	`selective_focus`	attends to only some tokens by pattern
`sparsity_pattern`	`focus_pattern`	strided/fixed/learned selection method
`mixture_of_depths`	`skip_layers`	dynamically skips layers per input
`attention_dropout` / `hidden_dropout`	`focus_forget_rate` / `layer_forget_rate`	dropout on attention vs. general layers
`stochastic_depth`	`layer_skip_rate`	randomly skips whole layers in training
`mixup_alpha`	`blend_strength`	blends two training examples together
`cutmix`	`patch_swap`	vision-specific patch swapping
`gradient_checkpointing`	`memory_saver_mode`	trades compute time for lower training memory
`ema_decay`	`smoothing_factor`	smoothed running average of weights
`z_loss_coef`	`logit_stabilizer`	prevents unstable output score growth
`beta_kl`	`alignment_pull`	how strongly kept close to original behavior during RLHF
`reward_clip`	`reward_limit`	caps extreme RLHF reward values
`ppo_clip_ratio`	`update_limit`	caps how much one RLHF update can shift behavior
`preference_loss`	`preference_method`	DPO/ORPO/KTO alignment approach
`reference_model`	`comparison_baseline`	frozen copy for measuring alignment drift
`retriever_type`	`search_style`	dense/sparse/hybrid retrieval
`embedding_dim`	`vector_size`	retrieval embedding vector size
`reranker_model`	`result_sorter`	re-orders retrieved documents by relevance
`vector_db`	`memory_store`	database holding retrieval vectors
`quantization`	`compression_type`	int8/int4/GPTQ/AWQ weight shrinking method
`bits`	`precision_bits`	detail per weight (4 or 8)
`group_size`	`compression_block`	weights compressed together per group
`pruning_sparsity`	`trim_ratio`	fraction of weights removed
`lora_target_modules`	`finetune_targets`	which layers a fine-tune may touch
Allocating memory for a specific model — three levels of control:
```
// 1. Preset — simplest, framework configures everything underneath
model.set_memory(preset: "long_chat")   // → sliding window + RoPE scaling + int8 KV cache + RAG, bundled

// 2. Explicit — allocate each feature individually
model.memory.configure(
    span: 32000, focus_width: 4096, position_scale: 500000,
    remember_past: true, cache_precision: "int8"
)
model.memory.enable("retrieval", docs_recalled: 5, retrieval_bite_size: 512,
    source: "huggingface://my_knowledge_base")

// 3. Per-tier — adjust just one piece of an existing model
existing_model.memory.enable("retrieval", docs_recalled: 3)
existing_model.memory.disable("sliding_window")
existing_model.memory.status()   // → current allocation snapshot

// 4. Advisor — framework recommends, developer approves explicitly (never silent)
let suggestion = qai.suggest_memory_strategy(target_context: "32k", hardware: qai.detect_hardware())
model.memory.apply(suggestion)
```
