63. Optimization, Model Families & Capability Extraction
Syntax correction: built-in Types never need importing — `qai.build(technique: "regression")` already knows what "regression" means. `import` is only for someone else's published custom technique:
```
let model = qai.build(technique: "regression")   // no import needed for built-ins
import "community/my_custom_technique"            // only for third-party custom techniques
let model = qai.build(technique: MyCustomTechnique)
```
Pruning — automatic by default; the developer sets the dial and scope, not individual weights:
```
model.prune(target: 0.3)                                      // "remove 30%" — framework decides which weights
model.prune(target: 0.3, scope: "attention_layers")             // coarse control: WHERE
model.prune(target: 0.3, method: "magnitude" | "gradient_based" | "movement")   // WHICH importance metric
model.prune_preview(target: 0.3)                                // shows affected regions before committing
```
Real practice: an automatic importance score picks which weights go; hand-picking individual weights isn't realistic at scale.
Order-aware optimization pipeline (replaces the earlier flat option list):
```
let plan = qai.suggest_optimization(model, target: "runs on 4GB phone, keep accuracy above 90%")
// → recommends order: prune 25% → recovery finetune → quantize int8 → fuse layers, with reasoning shown

model.optimize(plan, keep_uncompressed_backup: true)
model.optimize_report()   // size/speed/accuracy tradeoff, before vs after

// Manual, step by step:
model.prune(0.25)
model.finetune(data, epochs: 1)   // recovery finetune, standard practice after lossy compression
model.quantize("int8")
model.fuse_layers()
```
Model families — one base model, multiple deployable sizes (the Gemini/Gemini Flash pattern):
```
let family = qai.create_family(base_model,
    variants: [
        { name: "large", size: "100%" },
        { name: "flash", size: "20%", method: "distillation" },
        { name: "nano", size: "5%", method: "distillation" }
    ]
)
family.large / family.flash / family.nano
```
Capability extraction — surgical, not distillation: identifies which weight regions actually drive a specific capability (via concept-decomposition, Section 4) and discards everything else, rather than retraining a smaller student.
```
let coding_only = model.extract_capability("coding")
```
Should warn if the target capability is entangled with others (shares weights, can't be cleanly separated).
