64. Model Decomposition, Weight Editing & Skill Mechanics (Clarified)
`.edit()` — a real, concrete spec for direct manipulation of one decomposed section:
```
let section = model.decompose(by: "layer" | "magnitude" | "concept")["layer3"]
let editor = section.edit()

editor.set_weight(index: [0,5], value: 0.82)
editor.zero_out(indices: [12, 45, 90])
editor.scale(factor: 0.5)
editor.replace_with(other_section)
editor.commit()
```
Sections overview — see every decomposed section at once:
```
model.sections_overview()
// → { "layer1": {role: "input processing", weight_health: "stable"},
//     "layer3": {role: "reasoning", weight_health: "some dead weights"},
//     "output_layer": {role: "decision", skills_attached: ["rigging"]} }
```
`sections["x"].diff_from_original()` shows exactly what changed in one edited piece.
Skill mechanics — clarified precisely. A skill does NOT retrain the base model. The base model's weights are read from, never written to. A skill is a tiny separate calculation added at one declared point in the forward pass:
```
skill_output = base_representation + (skill_matrix_A × skill_matrix_B × base_representation)
final_output = base_model.continue_from(skill_output)
```
Training a skill = only its own small A/B matrices update via backprop
Attaching = adding that small calculation into the forward pass at its declared `insertion_point`
Detaching = removing it — base model reverts exactly to its pre-attachment state
Full worked example:
```
let model = qai.build(technique: "diffusion", output_type: "3d")
model.train(mesh_dataset)   // good at generating characters, can't rig them

let rigging_skill = qai.skill.train(
    base: model, data: qai.dataset.stream("huggingface://rigged_characters"),
    insertion_point: "output_layer", epochs: 5
)   // base frozen throughout — only the skill's own adapter weights train

model.attach_skill(rigging_skill)
model.generate("a walking character").rig()
```
`qai.suggest_insertion_point(base_model, skill_goal: "rigging")` can recommend where a new skill should tap in.
