66. Live Streams, Learning Paradigms & Current Generative Techniques
Live raw input — an ordinary Input stream, no learning implied:
```
let camera_feed = qai.input.connect_stream(source: "camera", type: "video")
model.process(camera_feed)                    // pure inference on a continuous feed
model.online_learn(feed: camera_feed, memory_buffer: true)   // OPT-IN separate layer if weights should also keep updating
```
Online/incremental learning updates model parameters continuously from a live stream rather than a fixed dataset; real systems must guard against catastrophic forgetting (losing old knowledge while adapting) and concept drift (the real-world patterns themselves shifting) — `memory_buffer: true` periodically re-tests against old data to guard against this.
Type vs. Technique vs. Learning Paradigm — three related but separate concepts:
```
let model = qai.build(type: "regression")              // ARCHITECTURE — Regression/CNN/RNN/Transformer/MoE
model.learning_technique()   // → "supervised", a sensible default, always overridable

let model = qai.build(type: "transformer", learning_technique: "self_supervised")
```
Each Type declares which learning paradigm(s) it's compatible with; mismatches produce a clear, corrective error, e.g.:
```
let model = qai.build(type: "transformer")
model.train(image_dataset)
// → Error: "Transformer's default input capability is 'text'. This dataset is images.
//    Did you mean type: 'diffusion' or type: 'vision_transformer'?"
```
Full learning-technique list: Supervised, Unsupervised, Self-Supervised, Semi-Supervised, Reinforcement, Online/Incremental, Transfer Learning, Few-Shot/Meta-Learning, Contrastive Learning, Imitation Learning, Curriculum Learning (as a full paradigm, not just a training-loop detail). `qai.learning_techniques_library()` browses all of them with which Types they typically pair with.
Current (2026) generative techniques beyond diffusion, as real distinct Types:
```
type FlowMatching extends Technique { }       // learns a direct noise-to-data vector field; now the default paradigm for image generation, more efficient than diffusion
type RectifiedFlow extends FlowMatching { }    // near-straight noise-to-data paths, fewer inference steps
type ConsistencyModel extends Technique { }    // maps noise directly to data in far fewer steps; trainable from scratch or distilled from diffusion
```
Video generation is generally image generation extended with a temporal dimension, often using a 3D VAE for combined spatial-temporal compression to keep frames consistent over time.
```
qai.family("image_video_generation")
// → Diffusion, FlowMatching, RectifiedFlow, ConsistencyModel, GAN, Autoregressive_pixel_space, VAE_based
```
