67. Bidirectional Model Communication & Multi-Model Networks
Bidirectional exchange ("debate"/"collaborate") — distinct from one-way `.pipe_to()`:
```
let channel = qai.connect_bidirectional(model_a, model_b, mode: "debate" | "collaborate" | "negotiate")
let result = channel.run(topic: "...", max_rounds: 5, until: fn(history) { history.last_two_agree() })
```
Explicit, developer-controlled multi-model wiring — no assumed shape:
```
let network = qai.network()
network.add(model_a, model_b, model_c)
network.route(model_a -> model_b)
network.route(model_b -> model_c)
network.route(model_c -> model_a)     // full loops allowed
network.rewire(model_b -> model_a)     // change routing later, anytime
```
Output ownership — an explicit choice per pipeline, never assumed:
```
qai.pipeline([model_a, model_b, model_c]).designate_output(model_c)           // one model's output is THE answer
qai.pipeline([model_a, model_b, model_c]).combine_outputs(strategy: "merge")   // all contribute, merged
qai.pipeline([model_a, model_b, model_c]).combine_outputs(strategy: "bundle")  // kept separate (Bundle, Section 38)
qai.pipeline([model_a, model_b, model_c]).combine_outputs(strategy: "vote")    // majority-agreement answer
```
Conditional routing is just ordinary code — no special DSL needed, since models are regular callable objects:
```
let decision = director_model.decide(topic)
if decision.needs_image {
    let img = image_model.generate(decision.image_prompt)
    output.attach(img)
}
```
`LearningTechnique` as its own formal interface, parallel to `Type` (Section 56), with the same editable/read-only discipline as Section 65:
```
learning_technique ReinforcementLearning {
    params { reward: f64 {editable:true}, penalty: f64 {editable:true}, gamma: f64 {alias:"future_importance",editable:true}, epsilon: f64 {alias:"exploration_rate",editable:true} }
    readonly { cumulative_reward: f64, episode_count: int }
}
learning_technique TransferLearning {
    params { source_model: Model, frozen_layers: [string], transfer_amount: f64 {alias:"carry_over_strength",editable:true} }
}
model.learning.reward = 10            // editable
model.learning.cumulative_reward()     // read-only, measured
```
General feedback-loop primitive — generalizes long-form video continuation (Section 22) to any "feed output back into itself" pattern (long story, extending image sequence, etc.):
```
qai.feedback_loop(
    model: video_model,
    carry: "last_frames",
    until: fn(state) { state.total_duration >= target_duration },
    on_iteration: fn(chunk, state) { state.append(chunk) }
)
```
Consistency as a general, explicit model property — not buried inside one technique:
```
model.consistency_reference
model.set_consistency_strength(0.8)
```
