68. Editing Core Model Logic ("Brain Logic")
Changing a model's actual internal logic — not just its parameters or hyperparameters — is done through `override`, already part of the Type system (Section 56), made concrete:
```
type VideoDiffusion {
    fn forward(current_frame) -> next_frame { /* default: predicts forward */ }
}
type ReverseFramePredictor extends VideoDiffusion {
    override fn forward(current_frame) -> previous_frame { /* genuinely different logic, not just different weights */ }
}
```
`override fn forward(...)` changes what KIND of thinking happens; training then finds good weights for that new logic — logic and learned weights are two separate things, and this is how you touch the first one.
Exporting custom-logic models — must bundle logic + weights, not weights alone:
```
model.export("my_model.qmodel")          // bundles custom logic (Type definition/code) AND weights together
model.export_weights_only("my_model.gguf")  // ONLY valid for unmodified built-in Types, where the logic is already known on the receiving end
```
Automated logic-variant search — tests structural variations of core logic automatically, not just hyperparameters. Corrected in Section 70: takes real, user-authored candidate Types, never a hardcoded preset list of mutations.
```
type MyIdeaA extends VideoDiffusion { override fn forward(frame) -> next_frame { /* predicts backward, author's own idea */ } }
type MyIdeaB extends VideoDiffusion { override fn forward(frame) -> next_frame { /* a different author idea */ } }

let variants = qai.search_logic_variants(
    base: VideoDiffusion,
    candidates: [MyIdeaA, MyIdeaB],
    evaluate_on: video_dataset,
    metric: "consistency_score"
)
variants.best()
```
Logic sandbox — cheap preview before committing to a full retrain:
```
let sandbox = model.logic_sandbox()
sandbox.try_override("forward", new_logic_fn)
sandbox.preview(sample_input)   // approximate result using existing weights, no full retrain
sandbox.commit()                  // now real, triggers proper retraining
```
