70. Open Logic Authoring — No Hardcoded Menus (Core Principle)
Standing rule for the whole document: anywhere a feature looks like "pick from this list," the correct version is "write your own function/Type and hand it to the same slot." Any list that exists should only be pre-shipped examples, never the ceiling.
Corrected logic-variant search — takes real, user-authored candidates, never a fixed preset list:
```
type MyIdeaA extends VideoDiffusion { override fn forward(frame) -> next_frame { /* any idea at all */ } }
type MyIdeaB extends VideoDiffusion { override fn forward(frame) -> next_frame { /* a different idea */ } }

qai.search_logic_variants(base: VideoDiffusion, candidates: [MyIdeaA, MyIdeaB], evaluate_on: data, metric: "consistency_score")
```
Open event/hook system — authors invent their own named hook points, nothing predefined:
```
type MyDiffusion extends Diffusion {
    fn forward(input) -> output {
        let midpoint = compute_something(input)
        emit("midpoint_reached", midpoint)          // author-invented event name
        return finish(midpoint)
    }
}
model.on("midpoint_reached", fn(data) { ... })       // anyone downstream can subscribe
```
Open custom checks/conditions — arbitrary user functions, not a menu of check types:
```
model.add_check(fn(state) { return state.loss < previous_epoch_loss * 2 })
```
Further open extensions:
User-defined composition operators: `qai.compose(logic_a, logic_b, combinator: fn(out_a, out_b) { /* your own blending idea */ })`
Parameterized logic templates: `type Flexible extends Diffusion { fn forward(input, lookback: int) { ... } }`
Live logic hot-swapping on a served model: `model.swap_logic(new_logic, zero_downtime: true)`
Community hook/event-name registry — lets common hook names converge by convention without the framework forcing it
