75. Mutable Weights, Remote Training & Self-Modification Safety
Logic makes weights genuinely mutable, not permanently frozen after training — a real, valuable capability that needs an equally real safety net.
Remote-compute-triggered training from inside logic:
```
model.logic {
    input(new_data)
    let job = qai.connect_remote_compute("kaggle" | "colab" | "own_cluster")
    let updated_weights = job.train(base: model, data: new_data, wait: false)

    on job.complete {
        let diff = model.preview_weight_diff(updated_weights)   // safety gate — review before accepting
        if diff.looks_safe() { model.apply_weights(updated_weights) }
        else { model.flag_for_review(diff) }
    }
    output(model.status())
}
```
Mutability is opt-in, never the default:
```
model.set_mutability("frozen" | "mutable")   // "frozen" is the safe default
```
Full weight-change audit trail:
```
model.weight_history()   // → [{ time, changed_by, diff_summary }, ...]
model.rollback_weights(to: "2026-08-20")
model.pin_as_stable("v4")                        // trusted fallback target
model.set_mutation_limit(max_changes_per_day: 3)  // caps runaway self-modification
```
Training itself IS written as logic — no hidden separate training step:
```
let vm = qai.connect_vm(sandboxed: true)
model.logic {
    input(task)
    let code = model.generate(task)
    let result = vm.run(code)
    if result.tests_passed { model.reinforce(code, reward: 1.0) } else { model.reinforce(code, reward: -1.0) }
    output(result)
}
```
Imitation learning by recording real demonstrations:
```
let screen_feed = qai.input.connect_stream(source: "screen", type: "video")
let input_feed = qai.input.connect_stream(source: "mouse_and_keyboard")
model.logic {
    input(demonstration_session)
    while demonstration_session.active {
        model.record_demonstration(state: screen_feed.capture(), action: input_feed.capture())
    }
    model.train(technique: "imitation_learning", data: model.recorded_demonstrations())
    output(model.status())
}
```
(Data collection needs no Type declared yet — the Type is chosen only when training actually begins.)
Thinking loop — repeated internal reasoning before committing to a final answer, matching how modern reasoning models work:
```
model.logic {
    input(task)
    var thought = model.think(task)
    while model.confidence(thought) < 0.9 {
        thought = model.think(task, previous_thought: thought)
    }
    output(thought)
}
```
Terminology note: repeated self-retraining on one's own gaps is continual learning / a self-improvement loop — not meta-learning, which specifically means "trained to adapt quickly to new, unseen tasks" (Section 66).
Whole-model freeze/unfreeze and capability-based skipping, from inside logic:
```
model.logic {
    input(prompt)
    let category = classifier_model.classify(prompt)
    if category != "video" { video_model.freeze() } else { video_model.unfreeze(); output(video_model.generate(prompt)); return }
    output(text_model.generate(prompt))
}
```
Lazy loading adapted per receiving device, from inside logic:
```
model.logic {
    input(request)
    if qai.detect_hardware().ram_available < 4.gb { model.set_loading_strategy("layer_stream") }
    output(model.generate(request))
}
```
