76. Dynamic Region Loading & Smart Memory Triage
`.qmodel` confirmed as the answer to "our own format" — needed specifically because GGUF can't carry logic:
```
model.export("my_model.qmodel")            // bundles logic AND weights together
model.export_weights_only("model.gguf")     // valid ONLY for models using unmodified built-in logic
```
Dynamic, per-request weight region loading — distinct from the one-time, permanent `extract_capability()` (Section 63):
```
model.logic {
    input(prompt)
    let topic = classifier_model.classify(prompt)
    let active_region = model.load_region(topic)   // only loads the weight region relevant to THIS request
    output(active_region.generate(prompt))
}
```
Smart memory triage logic — relevance-based keep/archive/delete, avoiding re-processing full history every time:
```
model.logic {
    input(message)
    let relevance = model.memory.relevance(message)

    if relevance > 0.5 { model.memory.retrieval.add(message) }
    else { qai.export_to_file(message, format: "markdown", path: "archive.md") }

    if model.memory.retrieval.has_stale_entries() { model.memory.retrieval.delete_stale() }

    let recent_context = model.memory.working.last(1)   // only the last exchange, not the whole history
    output(model.generate(message, context: recent_context))
}
```
Auto-summarization as a middle ground — `model.memory.summarize_and_compress(older_than: "10_messages")`, condense instead of fully drop
Live-adjustable relevance threshold — `model.memory.set_relevance_threshold(0.6)`
Archived content stays searchable — `model.memory.search_archive("markdown files")`
Memory-decision transparency — `model.memory.explain_decision(message)`
