85. Honest Assessment & Meta-Design Additions
Honest take on the overall design: the recurring open-interface pattern (Technique, Environment, Bridge, Renderer, Input/Output, logic hooks) reused consistently rather than accumulating special cases is the real strength — rarer than any single feature. The logic system specifically differs from orchestration frameworks like LangGraph/AutoGPT/CrewAI in kind, not just degree: those orchestrate around a frozen model; Quantum's logic reaches inside it (weights, `forward()`, skills, retraining) — a genuine architectural difference, though unproven at production scale the way those tools are.
Python-framework-instead-of-a-language tradeoff (honest note, not a plan change): a Python framework would be faster to build and adopt, but gives up the two real differentiators — "faster than Python because compiled" and "the logic block is real language syntax." Since real compiler infrastructure already exists (v3.x), that tradeoff favors staying the course.
Three-model self-play system (coder / reviewer-penalizer / researcher-asker) — a direct, valid extension of Section 14's role system:
```
let model = qai.build("combined")
model.add_role("coder", type: "transformer", goal: "write_code")
model.add_role("reviewer", type: "classifier", goal: "penalize_or_reward")
model.add_role("researcher", type: "transformer", goal: "generate_questions")
model.connect("researcher" -> "coder", channel: "question")
model.connect("coder" -> "reviewer", channel: "code")
model.connect("reviewer" -> "coder", channel: "reward_or_penalty")
model.set_evaluator(fn(code) { return run_tests(code) && reviewer.check(code) })
model.train(mode: "self_play", rounds: 1000)
```
`WeightEditorModel` — grounded in a real, established research concept: hypernetworks (a network that generates/edits another network's weights):
```
type WeightEditorModel extends Technique {
    fn analyze(target_weights) -> insight { ... }
    fn propose_edit(target_weights, goal: "improve_accuracy") -> new_weights { ... }
}
let editor = qai.build(type: "WeightEditorModel")
editor.train(on: many_past_weight_edits_and_their_outcomes)
let improved = editor.propose_edit(some_model.weights, goal: "reduce_bias")
```
