103. Additional Training Strategies
```
model.train(data, strategy: "data_parallel")       // same model copied across devices, results averaged
model.train(data, strategy: "tensor_parallel")       // one layer's math split across devices, for layers too big for one
model.train(data, strategy: "pipeline_parallel")      // different layers live on different devices, staged flow
model.train(data, strategy: "zero_offload")             // shards optimizer state/gradients across devices, cuts per-device memory

model.train(data, progressive: { start_size: 64, end_size: 256, grow_every: "10 epochs" })   // progressive resizing
model.train(data, swa: true, swa_start_epoch: 40)                                              // Stochastic Weight Averaging
qai.population_train(model, population_size: 8, evolve_every: "5 epochs")                       // Population-Based Training
model.predict(x, test_time_adapt: true)                                                            // test-time adaptation, per-input
model.train(data, optimizer: "sam", base_optimizer: "adam")                                          // Sharpness-Aware Minimization
model.finetune(data, unfreeze_schedule: { epoch_5: "last_layer", epoch_10: "last_3_layers", epoch_20: "all" })   // progressive unfreezing

model.train(
    data: large_dataset,
    strategy: "sequential_layers",   // train one layer's weights at a time, others stay on disk until their turn
    ram_budget: "16GB",
    offload_to: "disk"
)
```
Blind spots addressed:
Cross-hardware reproducibility — `qai.numerics.set_determinism_mode("strict" | "fast")` — floating-point results can vary slightly across GPU models
Fault tolerance — `model.train(strategy: "data_parallel", fault_tolerance: "auto_resume_from_last_checkpoint")` — recover from a node crash without losing all progress
Energy-cost-aware scheduling — `qai.schedule_training(model, data, prefer_hours: "off_peak")`
Network bandwidth awareness in distributed setups — often the real bottleneck, not compute; not yet surfaced/optimized for
