109. Generation Sampling, Model Loading & Tokenizer Details
```
model.generate(prompt, top_p: 0.9, top_k: 50, repetition_penalty: 1.2, frequency_penalty: 0.5, presence_penalty: 0.3, do_sample: true, seed: 42)

model.generate(prompt, max_new_tokens: 200)   // limits ONLY newly generated text
model.generate(prompt, max_length: 200)         // limits prompt + generated text COMBINED — an important, easily confused distinction

tokenizer.encode(text, padding_side: "left"|"right", truncation_side: "left"|"right", add_special_tokens: true)

qai.load("huggingface://some-model",
    revision: "a1b2c3d", trust_remote_code: false,   // security-relevant: refuses to execute bundled custom code unless explicitly allowed (Section 33)
    local_files_only: false, cache_dir: "~/.qai/cache", device_map: "auto")

model.train(data,
    eval_steps: 500, save_steps: 500, logging_steps: 100,
    dataloader_num_workers: 4, resume_from_checkpoint: true,
    max_grad_norm: 1.0, adam_beta1: 0.9, adam_beta2: 0.999, adam_epsilon: 1e-8,
    class_weights: {"rare_class": 3.0})
```
Notably important, not just cosmetic: sampling controls (used in essentially every real text-generation call) and `trust_remote_code` (a genuine, documented security concern with downloaded models).
