111. Reproducibility, Splitting & Sharing Details
```
model.train(data, early_stopping_patience: 3, early_stopping_min_delta: 0.001)
model.train(data, warmup_ratio: 0.1)   // first 10% of total steps, regardless of dataset size

model.set_label_mapping(label2id: {"positive":0,"negative":1}, id2label: {0:"positive",1:"negative"})   // keeps labels in sync everywhere, including .explain()

qai.dataset.split(data, train: 0.8, test: 0.2, stratify_by: "label")   // preserves class balance, avoids a common random-split mistake

qai.set_global_seed(42)   // one seed covering data shuffling, weight init, dropout — not just the model
qai.set_log_level("silent"|"warning"|"info"|"debug")

model.push_to_registry("my-username/my-model", private: false)

qai.dataset.load("huge_file.csv", mmap: true)   // reads on demand from disk, never loads the whole file into memory
```
Notably important: stratified splitting and the global seed — an unstratified split silently skewing results, and "reproducible except the data shuffle used a different seed," are both classic, frequent real bugs.
